{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 7769957715678686303, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 611, "mtime": 1791871702.4699762, "sha256": "d229b44353150f9f9f492a78ada7f7d30e8e443e2616a0928aadc094cbb4ab31"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 327, "mtime": 1791871705.1541364, "sha256": "2ec599a292ceac2f579c3bebec15a3e3a6da104362595226824374d7c0a95b29"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/4/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/4/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running the tests.\nFixed: `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** `round(x, 2)` didn't do what the docstring promised (\"half up\"), for two reasons:\n- The float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so it rounds down.\n- Python's `round()` rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, not up. For example, `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): it now converts the float to a string first, which gives `\"2.675\"` as typed. It then rounds that decimal value to cents, with halves always rounding up.\n\n```python\nreturn float(Decimal(str(x)).quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))\n```\n\nIt still returns a float, so `add_vat`, the only caller, needs no change.\n\n**Check:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, covering `2.675 \u2192 2.68`, `0.125 \u2192 0.13`, `-2.675 \u2192 -2.68` and `2.674 \u2192 2.67`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the new test and the existing `test_split` directly with `python3`. Both passed.\n- I confirmed the old `round()` gives `2.67` and `0.12` for those inputs, so the test would have failed before the fix.\n- `add_vat(10)` still returns `12.0`.\n\n**Limitation:** this rounds the value the float displays as. In `add_vat`, `x * 1.2` is calculated in floating point first, and a product that lands just below a half-cent will round down. Calculating in `Decimal` throughout would fix that, but it's a bigger change than this bug needed.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 210308, "requests_cache_write": 50383, "requests_cost_usd": 0.3361966, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2107, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id"